Build proxy cache

What is Build proxy cache?

Build proxy cache is an alternative proxy for TeamCity builds running in IDA environment.
It combines features of old Build and Stream proxies with added ability of caching.
It is set up to allow HTTP/S connections as well as Stream (SSH) connections with single configuration.
It is also setup to allow connections to GCP.
Access is managed per project(s)/build configuration instead of per agent pool as with the old proxies.
Detailed documentation of Build proxy cache functionality.
When can Build proxy cache be used?

Build proxy cache can be used for every TeamCity build that requires connections to internal network as well as to external network (internet).

What are the specifics of Build proxy cache?

Build proxy cache requires to have special parameters setup in TeamCity build configuration, so TeamCity plugin knows that Build proxy cache is used instead of old Build proxy and creates or reuses proxy configuration for it when the build is triggered in TeamCity.
It also requires special agents from Default_instant agent pool.
Usage of Build proxy cache

Teamcity configuration

For enabling Build proxy cache plugin in your TeamCity project, you need to set/unset those parameters:

Set parameter buildProxyEnabled to true
param("buildProxyEnabled", "true")
This parameter tells Build proxy cache plugin that Build proxy cache is used and new or already existing proxy configuration should be either created or reused when new build is started in TeamCity.

Remove all default proxy settings (set all of them to be empty string "")
param("env.HTTP_PROXY", "")
param("env.HTTPS_PROXY", "")
param("env.HTTP_PROXY_HOST", "")
param("env.HTTPS_PROXY_HOST", "")
Those parameters ensure that no other Build proxy is used in your builds (by default those parameters are set, so the old Build proxy is used by default for every TeamCity build).

Streaming Proxy Configuration with Default Ports

When setting up a streaming proxy, forwarding default ports like SSH (22) or Kafka (9092) to multiple destinations is not straightforward. To circumvent this limitation, initiate your build configuration (your first build step) with the Streaming Proxy Forwarder which utilizes Docker's service discovery mechanism.

The Streaming Proxy Forwarder leverages docker compose files automatically generated by TeamCity builds:

teamcity.ida.avast.com
teamcity-gen.ida.avast.com
Use the streamer-docker-compose parameter to specify the artifact path, for example: docker_compose_files/XxxTesting_BuildCacheTests_JjDemo/docker-compose.yml.

Steps to Use Streaming Proxy Forwarder:

Configure the streaming proxy as you normally would.
Run your build step inside a Docker container
Attach the container to the streamer_stream-proxy-forwarder network with the following Additional run arguments: --network streamer_stream-proxy-forwarder
