ACL rules

How do I add new ACL rule for my TeamCity project(s)/build configuration?

You have two options:

! ONLY if you are able to sign your commits ! Create a fork of this repository, add ACL according to the defined rules, then create a PR.
If ACL checks pass successfully for your PR, write a request to merge your PR to our #help-re channel. Also request Default_instant agent pool to be assigned to your project(s)/build configuration.
If ACL checks failed for your PR, please follow instructions in Resolving issues with ACL tests section.
Create a Task BLD ticket in Corp Jira. Exactly describe, what accesses (URLs or Streams) you need to allow, for which project, that you need to assign Default_instant agent pool to your project, etc. Example BLD ticket
ACL rules definition

🚨 IMPORTANT: If someone relocates a TC Project or build configuration and changes its ID, it's essential to make the same change in this repository. Failure to do so will result in loss of access. 🚨

Rules are defined in the root folder of this project
ACL rule file has .yml extension and structure
Folder/ACL structure of rules has to respect TeamCity project structure and is case-sensitive
Folder always represents the most root project of your and should be named after it (for example for Re_QualysResourcesCheck_QualysResourcesCheck project the most root project is RE, so it's located under this folder)
If you are creating ACL configuration for TeamCity project, it should be named as ID of this project. In this case all child projects and build configurations of this project will use configuration of this project.
If you are creating ACL configuration for TeamCity build configuration, it should be named as ID of this build configuration. In this case only this build configuration will use those ACL rules.
Example for the TC build configuration

Blackduck / AgentTest / AgentTestBuild you should create rules in:

/build-proxy-acl/Blackduck/Blackduck_AgentTest.yml
Example of rules definition

includes:
  - /shared/default.yml
  - test/seznam.yml
allowed:
  - ports: 80 443
    protocols: http https
    cached: false
    methods: GET POST
    urls:
      - url: www.google.com
      - url: eu.httpbin.org/post
        methods: POST
      - url: eu.httpbin.org/get
        cached: true
        methods: GET
  - ports: 8022
    protocols: stream
    urls:
      - url: github.com:22
Legend

includes - (optional section) import/reuse already created configuration
base path is always that, where the main ACL config is located (for example /build-proxy-acl/WinDev/) for the WinDev_AvastClient_Eperimental.yml ACL config
configs located in the base path can be imported by simply typing their location/name in relation to the base path:
tests/seznam.yml for the WinDev_AvastClient_Eperimental.yml ACL config will be imported from /build-proxy-acl/WinDev/
configs located outside the base path can be imported by simply defining / at the start of a location of the config (this way root directory /build-proxy-acl/WinDev/tests/seznam.yml is taken as the base path)
/shared/default.yml for any ACL config will be imported from /build-proxy-acl/shared/default.yml
redirects - (optional section) define redirects for URLs and locations
hostname - (mandatory section) defines URL, which will be redirected.
!URL needs to be entered without location!
cname - (mandatory section) defines URL, to which the previous entered URL in hostname section will be redirected.
!URL needs to be entered without location!
paths - (optional section) define redirects locations of the previously defined URL.
path - (mandatory section) defines location, which will be redirected.
if only the root location / is defined, then location which is about to be redirected will be added to the end of the redirected location (this is used for the Artifactory repos redirects, which consist of location in Artifactory + location of the original source)
if the exact location (for example /index.php) is defined, then location is replaced and nothing is being appended.
target - (mandatory section) defines location, to which the previous entered location in path section will be redirected.
allowed - (optional section) defines custom rules
ports - (mandatory section) defines port values, on which URLs should be whitelisted.
if the protocol value will be stream, then only single port should be defined as it's mapped 1:1 with port defined in the url section!
Allowed values: <22, 65535> Writing styles:
string 80 443 without commas
list [80, 443] with commas
protocols - (optional section) defines protocols, which should be used for defined ports, case-insensitive.
if the protocol value is stream, then defined port is the port on which default port (defined in the url) is being mapped.

Allowed values: ["http", "https", "stream"] Writing styles:

string http https without commas
list [http, https] with commas
Ports/protocols mapping:

1:1 - number of defined ports needs to be the same as the number of defined protocols and are paired 1:1
many:1 - all defined ports are mapped to the single defined protocol (for example https)
1:auto - for each defined port protocol is assigned automatically (only works for http and https, if stream should be used, then protocols needs to be defined)
cached - (optional section) defines, if the responses should be cached or not, case-insensitive.
default value is false
applies to the whole ports section
Allowed values: true/false
methods - (optional section) defines HTTP methods, for which urls should be whitelisted, case-insensitive.
default value is GET HEAD POST PUT DELETE PATCH (for the compatibility reasons)
applies to the whole ports section
Allowed values: ["GET", "HEAD", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "OPTIONS", "PATCH"] Writing styles:
string GET POST without commas
list [GET, POST] with commas
urls - (mandatory section) defines custom URLs, which should be whitelisted with more specifying rules.
url - (mandatory section) defines custom URL.
url can be defined either with or without paths, examples teamcity-gen.ida.avast.com or teamcity-gen.ida.avast.com/project/XxxTesting_BuildProxyUtils, or as wildcard (only wildcards starting with '*' are supported because of SSL certificates), for example "*.googlesource.com"
!Wildcards need to be defined as string (between "")!
!No protocol should be defined here, example https://teamcity-gen.ida.avast.com!
if stream protocol was defined, then port to map needs to be defined after URL, example github.com:22
cached - (optional section) defines, if the responses should be cached or not, case-insensitive.
default value is false
applies to the single defined URL
Allowed values: true/false
methods - (optional section) defines HTTP methods, for which url should be whitelisted, case-insensitive.
default value is GET HEAD POST PUT DELETE PATCH
applies to the single defined URL
Allowed values: ["GET", "HEAD", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "OPTIONS", "PATCH"] Writing styles:
string GET POST without commas
list [GET, POST] with commas
regex - (mandatory section) defines custom URL with regex in place of a location.
regex is to be defined as the base URL with / separating the location part defined as PCRE style regex, for example dortovapohotovost.cz/^/(?:index)\.php(?:$|/), where dortovapohotovost.cz is the base URL, / is the location separator and ^/(?:index)\.php(?:$|/) is the regex itself.
!No protocol should be defined here, example https://teamcity-gen.ida.avast.com!
cached - (optional section) defines, if the responses should be cached or not, case-insensitive.
default value is false
applies to the single defined URL
Allowed values: true/false
methods - (optional section) defines HTTP methods, for which url should be whitelisted, case-insensitive.
default value is GET HEAD POST PUT DELETE PATCH
applies to the single defined URL
Allowed values: ["GET", "HEAD", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "OPTIONS", "PATCH"] Writing styles:
string GET POST without commas
list [GET, POST] with commas
WARNING: both includes and allowed sections are optional, however at least one of them needs to be defined ( ACL config can't be empty)! WARNING: At least one URL needs to be always defined in the urls section!

Predefined most frequent rules

You can find rules that are always included (and are needed for basic functionality) in /build-proxy-acl/shared/auto-included.yml

Artifactory: /build-proxy-acl/shared/default.yml
Docker: /build-proxy-acl/shared/docker.yml
gcp-default: /build-proxy-acl/shared/gcp_default.yml
nuget: /build-proxy-acl/shared/nuget.yml
Resolving issues with ACL tests

Tests are running under Docker Ubuntu image. Please refer to the Build Log and scroll to the end of Step 2/6: Run ACL tests (Docker) step of this check to see what are the issues with your config. All warning and errors should be summarized in the last tests of this step.

If you encounter any issue with ACL checks TeamCity job, it may be one of the following issues:

YML failed to load / Wrong indentation Check, that your file is formatted and indented properly as the example. Tests should tell you the line, where the error occurs.
Unknown section defined Check, that every section and value in your file is named properly in lowercase. Refer to the Legend / How to section.
Wrong/duplicate value defined, wrong value definition Tests should output correct value for you, please refer to the tests output (for example port boundaries). Some of the values (for example url for stream) protocol can have only one value defined, and also stream ports can't be defined multiple times. Some values can be written either as a string or list, however some have only one and correct way how they can be written.
YML failed to validate Values in your config are not correct (tests should output which values and where to find them).
TeamCity project not found Teamcity project(s)/build configuration was not found for your ACL. Please create one, or if it's secret project, contact us in our #help-re channel to add your project to the project exception list.
nginx check failed There was an error when testing created ACL config for your project(s)/build configuration. There may be wrong nginx configuration in our template, nginx in our testing image or problem with proxy config translator itself. Contact us in our #help-re channel.
AssertionError: prerequisite failed. Some of the tests depend on each other, and when this dependency step fails, all other fail as well. Please contact us in our #help-re channel.
Any other issue If the issue you encounter does not have an explanation or resolve message or is not clear enough, please contact us in our #help-re channel.